        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Amory Lovins\n- Concepts: soft energy path\n- Organizations: Rocky Mountain Institute\n- Roles: energy policy analyst, physicist, environmental scientist, writer, Chairman, Chief Scientist\n- Topics: energy policy, energy efficiency, renewable energy, fossil fuels, nuclear fuels\n\nFacts:\n- Amory Bloch Lovins was born on November 13, 1947.\n- Amory Lovins is an American physicist, environmental scientist, writer, and energy policy analyst.\n- Amory Lovins is Chairman and Chief Scientist of the Rocky Mountain Institute.\n- In 1976, Amory Lovins coined the term soft energy path.\n- The soft energy path describes an alternative energy future in which energy efficiency and appropriate renewable energy sources steadily replace a centralized energy system based on fossil fuels and nuclear fuels.",
